   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I was asked below, back in June, as to the best place for feature requests for Rattle.<br><br>A new web site, <a href=\"http://connect-r.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://connect-r.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478580741000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2gXjySZMzU4T6rt-6bI6Ut\">http://connect-r.com</a>, is looking like a pretty good place to manage feature requests (and not just for Rattle but also for R). It is in the early stages of development but already is useful. I&#39;ve responded there to one Rattle feature request so far (now implemented in the latest release of Rattle). Feel free to add feature requests there - and use it as the central place which I will be monitoring. It also opens up the opportunity for others to contribute toward the request.<br><br>Even if you don&#39;t have a feature request it is useful to see which requests are most popular and hence perhaps more likely to be implemented (the request I resolved happened to be the most voted for request on the site so far!). So login and vote for a useful feature.<br><br>It seems early days for ConnectR but I will be adding a few of my own To Do items there to gauge interest in them.<br><br>Regards,<br>Graham</div>"
    ],
    [
